1
00:00:04,738 --> 00:00:06,272
Do you have cash?

2
00:00:06,339 --> 00:00:08,375
I didn't bring any cash.

3
00:00:11,811 --> 00:00:14,447
<i>The world is full of coincidences.</i>

4
00:00:14,514 --> 00:00:16,549
You can add hers with mine.

5
00:00:18,385 --> 00:00:19,252
No, you don't have to.

6
00:00:20,387 --> 00:00:21,621
<i>Twenty years ago,</i>

7
00:00:21,688 --> 00:00:24,958
<i>I had a fateful encounter with Mariko.</i>

8
00:00:25,725 --> 00:00:28,695
<i>I've always just watched over her.</i>

9
00:00:32,766 --> 00:00:34,934
<i>But now, she is finally aware of me.</i>

10
00:00:35,668 --> 00:00:36,336
NOTICE OF TRANSFER

11
00:00:36,403 --> 00:00:37,937
<i>Coincidences can be manufactured.</i>

12
00:00:38,972 --> 00:00:41,107
<i>A coincidence meant to make Mariko smile.</i>

13
00:00:41,708 --> 00:00:43,676
That old retro-style cafe
behind the office?

14
00:00:44,377 --> 00:00:45,512
<i>However…</i>

15
00:00:46,546 --> 00:00:51,618
<i>there are plenty of people who</i>
<i>approach Mariko and those who envy her.</i>

16
00:00:54,220 --> 00:00:57,991
<i>I have evidence that you used fraud</i>
<i>to obtain that partnership.</i>

17
00:00:58,058 --> 00:00:59,459
If you don't want this exposed,

18
00:00:59,526 --> 00:01:01,327
<i>withdraw from the new project.</i>

19
00:01:01,394 --> 00:01:03,329
Please, withdraw.

20
00:01:03,396 --> 00:01:05,331
-Please!
-What is wrong with you?

21
00:01:05,398 --> 00:01:07,367
Are you crazy or something?

22
00:01:07,434 --> 00:01:08,635
-Whoa!
-Please!

23
00:01:09,602 --> 00:01:11,504
<i>I must do what I need to do.</i>

24
00:01:12,405 --> 00:01:13,339
Murder?

25
00:01:14,407 --> 00:01:16,509
<i>Because I'm the one by Mariko's side.</i>

26
00:01:16,576 --> 00:01:17,944
I'M THE ONLY ONE BY MARIKO'S SIDE

27
00:01:18,011 --> 00:01:19,045
<i>I'll protect her.</i>

28
00:01:20,080 --> 00:01:21,481
19-JUN-26

29
00:01:27,087 --> 00:01:28,755
<i>That is the one thing I won't compromise.</i>

30
00:01:33,460 --> 00:01:35,695
NOSE COSMETICS

31
00:01:44,804 --> 00:01:46,573
<i>8:23 a.m.</i>

32
00:01:50,577 --> 00:01:53,012
<i>Mariko goes to work</i>
<i>at this exact time every morning.</i>

33
00:02:22,509 --> 00:02:25,678
BRAND BUSINESS DEPARTMENT

34
00:02:29,249 --> 00:02:31,284
-Good morning.
-Good morning.

35
00:02:31,351 --> 00:02:33,720
-Good morning.
-Good morning.

36
00:02:35,822 --> 00:02:39,025
<i>The very first thing she does when she</i>
<i>arrives at work is use alcohol sanitizer.</i>

37
00:02:39,092 --> 00:02:41,261
<i>After thoroughly wiping the keyboard,</i>

38
00:02:42,829 --> 00:02:46,266
<i>she checks the day's schedule,</i>
<i>right about now.</i>

39
00:02:46,966 --> 00:02:49,102
TOKYO DEPARTMENT STORE STATUS

40
00:02:52,472 --> 00:02:53,740
<i>Once she finishes that…</i>

41
00:02:54,874 --> 00:02:55,742
Here you go.

42
00:02:56,676 --> 00:02:58,878
Thank you. I was just
thinking I wanted one.

43
00:03:07,120 --> 00:03:08,855
<i>Mariko likes café lattes.</i>

44
00:03:13,526 --> 00:03:17,163
<i>I know everything about Mariko.</i>

45
00:03:19,899 --> 00:03:20,500
PROPOSAL TO INTRODUCE AI
INTO CLOUD SERVICES

46
00:03:20,567 --> 00:03:22,702
If we introduce AI into the cloud system,

47
00:03:22,769 --> 00:03:24,204
the work required to find documents

48
00:03:24,270 --> 00:03:27,073
from our vast library
should decrease significantly.

49
00:03:27,140 --> 00:03:29,108
No, to put that into effect,

50
00:03:29,175 --> 00:03:31,010
-the cost would be enormous--
-That is exactly

51
00:03:31,077 --> 00:03:32,812
the kind of thing
we should spend money on.

52
00:03:33,513 --> 00:03:34,781
If we revamp the system,

53
00:03:34,847 --> 00:03:38,151
it should reduce overtime by 40 hours
per year in each department.

54
00:03:39,986 --> 00:03:42,522
<i>That's easy for her to say.</i>

55
00:03:42,589 --> 00:03:45,024
From her standpoint, yes.

56
00:03:45,091 --> 00:03:47,327
I heard she just got
a new project approved too.

57
00:03:47,827 --> 00:03:51,130
Must be nice to have someone
backing you up.

58
00:03:57,971 --> 00:04:00,039
Don't worry about what they say.

59
00:04:01,908 --> 00:04:03,142
Oh, that.

60
00:04:03,876 --> 00:04:06,279
-I'm used to it.
-What?

61
00:04:07,113 --> 00:04:09,515
Wait, so are you still sad
about that thing?

62
00:04:10,917 --> 00:04:14,954
I never imagined dating would be harder
than college or job-hunting.

63
00:04:15,722 --> 00:04:16,889
Did something happen?

64
00:04:17,390 --> 00:04:18,891
No, nothing.

65
00:04:19,492 --> 00:04:21,761
I can't even keep a text conversation
going with anyone.

66
00:04:22,695 --> 00:04:25,698
In the end, they just want to get
on good terms with my father.

67
00:04:25,765 --> 00:04:27,467
A lot of them are like that.

68
00:04:28,201 --> 00:04:31,571
So they're not actually interested in you?

69
00:04:31,638 --> 00:04:33,172
Don't put it so bluntly.

70
00:04:34,540 --> 00:04:36,142
What about that guy from the other day?

71
00:04:36,209 --> 00:04:38,778
The one your grandmother
introduced to you.

72
00:04:41,047 --> 00:04:43,049
I almost didn't come.

73
00:04:43,116 --> 00:04:44,417
But I'm glad I came.

74
00:04:45,385 --> 00:04:48,855
What about his job? What does he do?

75
00:04:48,921 --> 00:04:50,456
Uh, he's a civil servant.

76
00:04:50,523 --> 00:04:52,925
A civil servant! That's great!

77
00:04:52,992 --> 00:04:54,694
-You think so?
-Yes!

78
00:04:55,461 --> 00:04:58,231
But we have had no developments
since then, either.

79
00:04:59,799 --> 00:05:03,703
Mariko, maybe you're not taking
any initiative at all?

80
00:05:03,770 --> 00:05:07,173
Are you making an effort to show them
who you really are?

81
00:05:13,880 --> 00:05:16,683
I plan to do it…

82
00:05:17,183 --> 00:05:18,951
Don't just plan, do it!

83
00:05:25,825 --> 00:05:26,793
Hello.

84
00:05:27,860 --> 00:05:29,162
Hello.

85
00:05:32,732 --> 00:05:34,934
-Hello.
-Hey there.

86
00:05:36,869 --> 00:05:38,805
Mariko, you can make it tomorrow, right?

87
00:05:38,871 --> 00:05:41,174
To the golf session with the CEO
of Keihin Department Store.

88
00:05:41,240 --> 00:05:42,842
-Yes.
-Actually,

89
00:05:42,909 --> 00:05:44,877
I received a call from them
just a moment ago.

90
00:05:44,944 --> 00:05:46,579
It seems one of them can't make it.

91
00:05:47,680 --> 00:05:49,415
Then shall we send
another one on our side?

92
00:05:49,482 --> 00:05:50,650
Asai, can you go?

93
00:05:50,717 --> 00:05:54,187
-No, I'm not really good at golf.
-<i>Mariko started golfing after she joined.</i>

94
00:05:54,687 --> 00:05:56,622
<i>It's good for entertaining guests.</i>

95
00:05:57,724 --> 00:05:58,791
<i>Mariko always prepares</i>

96
00:05:59,492 --> 00:06:02,328
<i>so that nothing at work</i>
<i>can catch her by surprise.</i>

97
00:06:04,597 --> 00:06:06,899
You still can't contact Tateiwa?

98
00:06:07,900 --> 00:06:08,735
No.

99
00:06:09,902 --> 00:06:11,471
What's going on?

100
00:06:16,776 --> 00:06:18,277
<i>And…</i>

101
00:06:20,413 --> 00:06:22,248
<i>I have my preparations too.</i>

102
00:06:35,561 --> 00:06:37,196
NOSE COSMETICS

103
00:06:37,263 --> 00:06:38,965
Sorry for bothering you.

104
00:06:39,031 --> 00:06:42,335
I'd like to speak with
the person in charge here.

105
00:06:42,869 --> 00:06:45,638
Please wait a moment. I'll ask.

106
00:06:50,076 --> 00:06:52,979
Well then, what can we help you with?

107
00:06:54,180 --> 00:06:55,848
Last night, around 10 p.m.,

108
00:06:55,915 --> 00:06:58,317
one of your directors,
Mr. Tsuyoshi Tateiwa,

109
00:06:58,384 --> 00:06:59,752
<i>was found dead.</i>

110
00:06:59,819 --> 00:07:00,787
What?

111
00:07:01,587 --> 00:07:03,956
Was it an accident?

112
00:07:04,023 --> 00:07:06,626
The police are investigating it
as a criminal case.

113
00:07:08,194 --> 00:07:11,764
When was the last time
you contacted Mr. Tateiwa?

114
00:07:12,432 --> 00:07:14,000
Two days ago.

115
00:07:14,066 --> 00:07:18,604
Actually, we were unable
to reach him as well, and we were worried.

116
00:07:21,073 --> 00:07:25,878
By the way, did Mr. Tateiwa
have any trouble at work,

117
00:07:25,945 --> 00:07:28,581
or did anyone hold grudges against him?

118
00:07:35,588 --> 00:07:39,625
This email was sent to me
the night before yesterday.

119
00:07:39,692 --> 00:07:40,626
This is evidence

120
00:07:40,693 --> 00:07:44,297
that Tateiwa was misappropriating
company expenses and other funds.

121
00:07:44,363 --> 00:07:47,800
-Do you have any idea who the sender is?
-I do not.

122
00:07:49,368 --> 00:07:52,472
The night two days ago,
that would be when the murder occurred.

123
00:07:52,538 --> 00:07:55,241
-May we have this data?
-Yes.

124
00:07:55,808 --> 00:07:58,711
We would also like to see
Mr. Tateiwa's desk.

125
00:07:58,778 --> 00:08:00,146
-Asai.
-Yes.

126
00:08:00,213 --> 00:08:01,814
-I'll show you.
-Thank you.

127
00:08:09,422 --> 00:08:11,691
This is terrible! This is terrible! Hey!

128
00:08:13,059 --> 00:08:14,494
-The police are here!
-What?

129
00:08:14,560 --> 00:08:15,428
The police?

130
00:08:16,796 --> 00:08:17,797
They say Mr. Tateiwa

131
00:08:18,931 --> 00:08:20,099
was murdered.

132
00:08:20,600 --> 00:08:23,202
-What? What do you mean he was murdered?
-No…

133
00:08:23,269 --> 00:08:25,204
I don't know the details, but…

134
00:08:26,472 --> 00:08:29,242
Look, the detectives are here.

135
00:08:49,896 --> 00:08:51,731
<i>Last night, at around 10 p.m.,</i>

136
00:08:51,797 --> 00:08:56,602
<i>a man was found collapsed on the street</i>

137
00:08:56,669 --> 00:08:58,971
<i>and was confirmed to have passed away.</i>

138
00:08:59,939 --> 00:09:02,842
<i>The incident happened after 5:00 p.m.</i>

139
00:09:02,909 --> 00:09:04,911
<i>A passerby reported</i>

140
00:09:04,977 --> 00:09:09,682
<i>finding a man collapsed</i>
<i>on a street in Shinagawa.</i>

141
00:09:09,749 --> 00:09:14,720
<i>The victim was Mr. Tsuyoshi Tateiwa.</i>

142
00:09:14,787 --> 00:09:17,590
<i>His body had several stab wounds,</i>

143
00:09:17,657 --> 00:09:20,860
<i>and the police are investigating this</i>
<i>as a homicide.</i>

144
00:09:32,371 --> 00:09:33,506
TSUYOSHI TATEIWA

145
00:09:36,609 --> 00:09:37,977
CREATING BACKUP

146
00:09:54,126 --> 00:09:56,062
ARE YOU SURE YOU WANT TO RESET THIS PC?

147
00:09:56,128 --> 00:09:57,063
RESETTING PC…

148
00:10:01,033 --> 00:10:03,769
SATORU HATANO RELEASED FROM PRISON

149
00:10:13,713 --> 00:10:16,115
If there is anything else
you wish to investigate,

150
00:10:16,182 --> 00:10:17,917
please contact me directly.

151
00:10:18,618 --> 00:10:21,053
Understood. Thank you very much.

152
00:10:22,321 --> 00:10:23,155
Good day.

153
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:36,936
Those incriminating documents,
sent anonymously…

154
00:10:37,003 --> 00:10:38,904
I'd bet they were sent by the killer.

155
00:11:00,593 --> 00:11:03,029
COMPANY DIRECTOR FOUND DEAD ON STREET

156
00:11:03,095 --> 00:11:04,697
DEEMED HOMICIDE

157
00:11:07,466 --> 00:11:08,834
Here, this is on the house.

158
00:11:09,969 --> 00:11:13,005
You don't seem to be focusing
very well on your work today.

159
00:11:15,141 --> 00:11:16,008
Thank you very much.

160
00:11:17,910 --> 00:11:19,311
You're that guy's boss, right?

161
00:11:20,046 --> 00:11:21,414
-That guy?
-Sota Yukimura.

162
00:11:23,449 --> 00:11:24,784
Yes. Are you acquaintances?

163
00:11:24,850 --> 00:11:27,186
Yes, yes, we both
went to Futasubashi University.

164
00:11:30,589 --> 00:11:32,358
-Futasubashi, I went there too.
-Oh, here he is.

165
00:11:32,425 --> 00:11:35,127
Hey, don't say anything you don't need to.

166
00:11:35,194 --> 00:11:37,263
It's fine. She'd find out
eventually anyway.

167
00:11:37,329 --> 00:11:38,931
We were both in the Faculty of Commerce.

168
00:11:38,998 --> 00:11:40,566
I went there too!

169
00:11:40,633 --> 00:11:43,869
We both took a gap year, so we're
one academic year below you, though.

170
00:11:43,936 --> 00:11:46,405
-Oh, really?
-I've wanted to talk to you

171
00:11:46,472 --> 00:11:47,907
ever since university.

172
00:11:47,973 --> 00:11:49,875
Oh, I'm Tomoya Sagara, by the way.

173
00:11:49,942 --> 00:11:51,944
-Okay.
-Mariko, what do you think of this guy--

174
00:11:52,011 --> 00:11:53,713
That's enough.

175
00:11:53,779 --> 00:11:55,081
-What, what?
-Go back to work.

176
00:11:55,147 --> 00:11:56,615
I'm going, all right, all right.

177
00:11:57,750 --> 00:12:00,186
I get it, okay? Want a cookie?

178
00:12:00,252 --> 00:12:01,487
No.

179
00:12:11,964 --> 00:12:14,100
Don't be mad. I said I was sorry.

180
00:12:15,067 --> 00:12:17,269
I was trying to be your wingman,

181
00:12:17,336 --> 00:12:19,271
giving you two a chance
to get to know each other.

182
00:12:19,338 --> 00:12:21,640
Look, consider this an apology.

183
00:12:21,707 --> 00:12:24,577
You liar. Bet you just talked
and couldn't stop.

184
00:12:26,178 --> 00:12:27,613
It's fine.

185
00:12:27,680 --> 00:12:30,716
I know what's okay to say and what's not.

186
00:12:33,185 --> 00:12:35,454
If I told her you've loved her
for 25 years straight,

187
00:12:35,521 --> 00:12:37,490
she'd find it creepy
and reject you instantly.

188
00:12:37,556 --> 00:12:39,358
I would absolutely never say that.

189
00:12:43,362 --> 00:12:45,431
Don't worry.

190
00:12:46,198 --> 00:12:49,602
I won't steal your one and only love.

191
00:12:49,668 --> 00:12:51,737
What? Mariko wouldn't
fall for you, Tomoya.

192
00:12:51,804 --> 00:12:54,840
What's that about? You don't know that.

193
00:12:54,907 --> 00:12:56,942
I know everything about Mariko.

194
00:12:58,310 --> 00:12:59,845
Everything, huh…

195
00:13:01,180 --> 00:13:05,184
Well then, do you know
who Mariko's closest friend is?

196
00:13:05,251 --> 00:13:06,485
Her colleague and secretary, Izumi.

197
00:13:06,552 --> 00:13:07,386
That was fast.

198
00:13:09,088 --> 00:13:11,457
Izumi is a senior colleague
three years older than Mariko,

199
00:13:11,524 --> 00:13:15,194
but since Mariko is the manager,
she is her most trusted subordinate.

200
00:13:16,262 --> 00:13:18,197
While they have
a professional relationship,

201
00:13:18,764 --> 00:13:22,735
she is a rare, friend-like figure
with whom Mariko can be herself.

202
00:13:23,402 --> 00:13:26,305
Then what about outside of work?

203
00:13:26,372 --> 00:13:28,808
Like how she spends
long holidays and stuff.

204
00:13:30,309 --> 00:13:33,879
Mariko doesn't take much paid leave…

205
00:13:35,481 --> 00:13:38,217
Oh, but for New Year's, she spent it
in London with her grandmother.

206
00:13:39,485 --> 00:13:42,321
You could see fireworks
from the Thames River cruise.

207
00:13:42,388 --> 00:13:43,923
They were beautiful.

208
00:13:45,224 --> 00:13:46,458
Did you go too…

209
00:13:48,828 --> 00:13:50,462
No, never mind.

210
00:13:52,064 --> 00:13:54,033
I don't really want to know. It's scary.

211
00:13:55,534 --> 00:13:59,839
When it comes to Mariko, I know
everything, and I understand everything.

212
00:14:02,074 --> 00:14:03,275
I wonder.

213
00:14:04,577 --> 00:14:08,147
-What?
-This all sounds very one-sided to me.

214
00:14:08,214 --> 00:14:09,515
Would she really date you?

215
00:14:10,616 --> 00:14:11,951
What?

216
00:14:12,451 --> 00:14:15,254
-I'm not planning on--
-And what's that you've been doing?

217
00:14:17,690 --> 00:14:18,858
Golf?

218
00:14:23,162 --> 00:14:25,297
MARIKO

219
00:14:31,136 --> 00:14:33,405
Nice shot!

220
00:14:33,472 --> 00:14:34,840
Nice shot!

221
00:14:35,641 --> 00:14:38,978
-Sent it flying, like always!
-All right!

222
00:14:54,226 --> 00:14:57,630
-Nice shot!
-Your direction is perfect!

223
00:14:57,696 --> 00:14:58,764
Thank you very much.

224
00:14:59,665 --> 00:15:01,000
Do you have a professional coach?

225
00:15:01,066 --> 00:15:03,035
I went to a place called Koto Golf Club.

226
00:15:04,270 --> 00:15:05,905
I used to go there too.

227
00:15:05,971 --> 00:15:08,874
Oh, it's nice there, isn't it?
It's close to the company,

228
00:15:08,941 --> 00:15:10,676
and they offer cheap personal lessons.

229
00:15:11,477 --> 00:15:12,778
That's true.

230
00:15:14,980 --> 00:15:18,717
Man, where do you train, Jinno?

231
00:15:21,387 --> 00:15:23,923
Sorry for asking you
to come on such short notice.

232
00:15:24,456 --> 00:15:27,893
No one else in our department
could play golf, so it was a huge help.

233
00:15:27,960 --> 00:15:29,028
Not at all.

234
00:15:31,230 --> 00:15:32,765
Do you play often?

235
00:15:33,499 --> 00:15:36,702
I often go to the driving range
at Koto Golf Club.

236
00:15:38,103 --> 00:15:41,006
<i>I wonder if a lot of people</i>
<i>from our company go there?</i>

237
00:15:41,540 --> 00:15:43,676
<i>That might be the case.</i>

238
00:15:50,516 --> 00:15:52,251
<i>Playing golf with Mariko…</i>

239
00:15:53,619 --> 00:15:56,221
<i>To think such a day would come.</i>

240
00:15:57,623 --> 00:16:00,659
<i>Am I about to be called to heaven? No,</i>

241
00:16:01,760 --> 00:16:03,696
<i>perhaps I have already been called.</i>

242
00:16:06,098 --> 00:16:07,700
<i>This is heaven.</i>

243
00:16:15,307 --> 00:16:17,543
Nice shot!

244
00:16:29,788 --> 00:16:32,691
I think this one would be better.

245
00:16:34,226 --> 00:16:35,194
Thank you.

246
00:16:48,774 --> 00:16:50,976
-Nice one!
-Nice one!

247
00:17:00,886 --> 00:17:03,956
<i>To think such a day would come…</i>

248
00:17:07,393 --> 00:17:10,029
Isn't your company
having it rough right now?

249
00:17:10,095 --> 00:17:12,698
You know, with that director,
Tateiwa, was it?

250
00:17:12,765 --> 00:17:14,366
Yes.

251
00:17:14,433 --> 00:17:18,003
We pulled some strings to keep
the company name out of the news for now.

252
00:17:18,904 --> 00:17:22,508
Well, the weekly magazines
will probably find out eventually, though.

253
00:17:22,574 --> 00:17:24,243
Well,

254
00:17:24,309 --> 00:17:27,746
a murder case is no laughing matter.

255
00:17:27,813 --> 00:17:31,283
It'd be terrifying if the killer
turned out to be someone close to him.

256
00:17:35,921 --> 00:17:37,089
Yes, exactly.

257
00:17:37,156 --> 00:17:40,893
Thankfully, our brand for young people
called VELEL is performing well.

258
00:17:40,959 --> 00:17:43,228
I know. I saw an article saying that

259
00:17:43,295 --> 00:17:46,198
while the industry as a whole
is struggling to establish brand loyalty,

260
00:17:46,265 --> 00:17:49,435
VELEL has maintained
an upward trend since its release.

261
00:17:51,303 --> 00:17:52,838
Actually, it has been decided

262
00:17:52,905 --> 00:17:56,008
that we will be launching
a new skincare line from VELEL.

263
00:17:56,542 --> 00:18:00,112
We would be very grateful to have
your support, Jinno.

264
00:18:00,179 --> 00:18:03,015
Shall we set up
an independent counter at our place?

265
00:18:03,649 --> 00:18:05,350
Yes, please!

266
00:18:06,452 --> 00:18:10,055
Your father and I
have been friends for over half a century,

267
00:18:10,122 --> 00:18:13,692
so our department store
will give you full support.

268
00:18:13,759 --> 00:18:14,793
Thank you very much.

269
00:18:15,294 --> 00:18:17,963
My, how impressive, how impressive.

270
00:18:19,064 --> 00:18:22,201
Nose Cosmetics is secure
with such a splendid successor.

271
00:18:22,267 --> 00:18:23,102
Well,

272
00:18:23,168 --> 00:18:25,938
I only made her a director
because she's my daughter.

273
00:18:26,004 --> 00:18:27,005
She still has a long way to go.

274
00:18:32,678 --> 00:18:36,281
You've known each other for over 50 years.
What relationship do you have?

275
00:18:36,348 --> 00:18:39,551
We're in a Gin-chan,
Jin-chan kind of friendship.

276
00:18:40,352 --> 00:18:41,753
That's right.

277
00:18:41,820 --> 00:18:45,090
I didn't think Jin-chan
would rise this high, though.

278
00:18:45,157 --> 00:18:46,758
Well, I'm glad we stayed on good terms.

279
00:18:46,825 --> 00:18:48,360
The feeling is mutual.

280
00:18:52,965 --> 00:18:54,633
Just this way.

281
00:18:55,367 --> 00:18:58,537
You did great, Jin-chan.

282
00:19:00,506 --> 00:19:02,474
-Thank you for today.
-Likewise.

283
00:19:08,714 --> 00:19:12,651
Great work. Thank you for today.
Let's meet again.

284
00:19:13,719 --> 00:19:15,687
Yes. Thank you very much.

285
00:19:15,754 --> 00:19:18,123
-Well then, I'll be leaving.
-Okay.

286
00:19:18,190 --> 00:19:19,024
See you.

287
00:19:25,531 --> 00:19:26,798
Yukimura, I'll give you a ride.

288
00:19:30,135 --> 00:19:30,969
What?

289
00:19:57,996 --> 00:19:59,031
You must be tired, right?

290
00:19:59,598 --> 00:20:02,367
-Sorry, I know it's your day off.
-No, no.

291
00:20:02,434 --> 00:20:03,502
That's not why.

292
00:20:15,948 --> 00:20:18,984
At what age did you start drinking coffee?

293
00:20:20,352 --> 00:20:22,354
That was a boring question. Sorry.

294
00:20:23,889 --> 00:20:25,090
Um…

295
00:20:26,091 --> 00:20:27,793
I think it was in elementary school?

296
00:20:28,694 --> 00:20:32,631
I think I snuck a sip of what
my mother was drinking.

297
00:20:34,700 --> 00:20:38,503
Oh, but I didn't start liking it
until I became an adult.

298
00:20:38,570 --> 00:20:40,372
-I like cafes, so that's why.
-Oh,

299
00:20:40,439 --> 00:20:42,007
I like cafes too.

300
00:20:42,774 --> 00:20:44,776
Um, I like how you're in the same space,

301
00:20:44,843 --> 00:20:48,280
but it feels like everyone
is in their own world.

302
00:20:49,848 --> 00:20:52,184
-I get that. I feel the same way.
-Oh?

303
00:20:53,352 --> 00:20:54,219
You do?

304
00:20:55,187 --> 00:20:57,422
Well, ever since I was a kid,

305
00:20:57,990 --> 00:21:00,225
I've liked looking at apartment buildings
from a distance.

306
00:21:00,792 --> 00:21:01,994
Apartment buildings?

307
00:21:02,060 --> 00:21:05,397
When those concrete-enclosed boxes
are born into this world,

308
00:21:05,464 --> 00:21:10,202
people who were living separate lives
fit neatly and politely into them.

309
00:21:10,269 --> 00:21:13,572
In that collective nature,
I felt a kind of beauty.

310
00:21:13,639 --> 00:21:15,807
That same feeling
is packed into cafes too.

311
00:21:16,508 --> 00:21:19,177
No one knows each other,

312
00:21:19,244 --> 00:21:21,046
but in the way that everyone

313
00:21:21,546 --> 00:21:24,616
gathers in a single space
and quietly shares time together,

314
00:21:25,617 --> 00:21:27,386
I feel a sense of romance.

315
00:21:31,923 --> 00:21:33,191
I'm talking too much, aren't I?

316
00:21:34,426 --> 00:21:36,028
I don't mind.

317
00:21:42,734 --> 00:21:43,735
Sorry.

318
00:21:48,740 --> 00:21:50,375
We surprisingly have a lot in common.

319
00:21:51,843 --> 00:21:52,778
Same university, too.

320
00:21:53,945 --> 00:21:59,084
Yes, uh, well, I barely managed
to slip in after a gap year.

321
00:21:59,985 --> 00:22:01,586
I barely got in too.

322
00:22:03,221 --> 00:22:06,325
But for some reason,
I've had a lucky life.

323
00:22:08,093 --> 00:22:11,463
Even on the day of the entrance exam,
I messed up,

324
00:22:12,030 --> 00:22:13,465
but I got lucky and passed.

325
00:22:13,532 --> 00:22:15,100
I don't think it was luck.

326
00:22:15,634 --> 00:22:19,004
You studied so hard.
It was your own ability.

327
00:22:20,105 --> 00:22:24,176
I mean, you just lost
your exam admission ticket.

328
00:22:24,242 --> 00:22:25,711
It doesn't mean you'd fail, right?

329
00:22:28,380 --> 00:22:30,415
What? Did I mention a ticket?

330
00:22:34,286 --> 00:22:35,220
No, uh…

331
00:22:37,522 --> 00:22:39,358
I just figured, messing up on exam day

332
00:22:39,958 --> 00:22:43,662
would mean losing
or dropping your exam ticket.

333
00:22:46,264 --> 00:22:47,232
Oh, okay.

334
00:22:56,641 --> 00:22:58,410
In other words, what I wanted to say

335
00:22:59,578 --> 00:23:01,380
is that both university
and your current job

336
00:23:02,848 --> 00:23:05,217
are results you grabbed
through real effort…

337
00:23:07,519 --> 00:23:09,287
and not luck at all.

338
00:23:11,923 --> 00:23:13,959
Sorry for speaking like I know everything.

339
00:23:16,027 --> 00:23:18,363
Everyone else says differently, though.

340
00:23:20,465 --> 00:23:23,635
Well, I only get to see clients
because my father is backing me up.

341
00:23:23,702 --> 00:23:25,203
So I don't blame them.

342
00:23:30,575 --> 00:23:32,444
I wonder why I'm telling you this.

343
00:23:33,111 --> 00:23:33,945
It's fine.

344
00:23:54,566 --> 00:23:56,168
<i>July 25th.</i>

345
00:23:56,868 --> 00:24:00,806
<i>Today, several things that should</i>
<i>have been impossible, no,</i>

346
00:24:01,606 --> 00:24:05,277
<i>things I've always waited for,</i>
<i>have finally happened.</i>

347
00:24:14,486 --> 00:24:15,654
JULY 25

348
00:24:15,720 --> 00:24:19,057
<i>It makes me realize</i>
<i>that life is connected.</i>

349
00:24:20,025 --> 00:24:23,361
<i>Because I started playing golf back then,</i>

350
00:24:23,428 --> 00:24:26,965
<i>it led to me being invited</i>
<i>to the client game today.</i>

351
00:24:33,805 --> 00:24:35,307
MARIKO

352
00:24:35,373 --> 00:24:38,410
FIRST TIME PLAYING GOLF IN A WHILE
THE WEATHER WAS GREAT

353
00:24:43,782 --> 00:24:44,716
<i>But…</i>

354
00:24:49,588 --> 00:24:52,357
<i>if life is connected…</i>

355
00:24:52,858 --> 00:24:54,259
JAPONICA WORKBOOK

356
00:24:55,360 --> 00:24:56,661
<i>…then it's possible…</i>

357
00:24:58,129 --> 00:25:00,098
<i>that the past will catch up with you.</i>

358
00:25:03,134 --> 00:25:04,169
<i>Today,</i>

359
00:25:05,136 --> 00:25:07,405
<i>I overheard something outrageous.</i>

360
00:25:07,472 --> 00:25:10,475
You got me good today, Jin-chan!

361
00:25:10,542 --> 00:25:11,843
Oh, by the way,

362
00:25:12,444 --> 00:25:14,746
I heard Hatano was released
from prison, right?

363
00:25:15,780 --> 00:25:16,681
Yes…

364
00:25:16,748 --> 00:25:19,918
Him, kidnapping someone…

365
00:25:19,985 --> 00:25:21,486
I still can't believe it.

366
00:25:22,687 --> 00:25:25,123
It looks like he's telling the weekly mags
lots of things.

367
00:25:25,690 --> 00:25:26,625
Be careful.

368
00:25:27,158 --> 00:25:29,928
It was a long time ago, but he might talk
about you too.

369
00:25:32,898 --> 00:25:34,833
<i>This man named Hatano…</i>

370
00:25:34,900 --> 00:25:35,901
SERIAL KIDNAPPER, 1 DEATH

371
00:25:40,939 --> 00:25:43,375
Somebody! Somebody help!

372
00:25:43,441 --> 00:25:46,311
-<i>Though Mariko's kidnapping was thwarted,</i>
-No! No!

373
00:25:47,646 --> 00:25:49,948
<i>he kidnapped five other children</i>

374
00:25:50,482 --> 00:25:53,985
<i>and murdered one who tried to escape.</i>

375
00:25:54,052 --> 00:25:55,587
WEAPON CONFISCATED AT HOME

376
00:25:55,654 --> 00:25:56,688
HATANO SENTENCED TO 25 YEARS

377
00:25:56,755 --> 00:26:00,258
<i>It was reported that</i>
<i>he stated he targeted children</i>

378
00:26:00,325 --> 00:26:01,893
<i>of wealthy families,</i>

379
00:26:02,394 --> 00:26:03,228
GINJIRO NOSE

380
00:26:03,295 --> 00:26:07,432
<i>but Mariko's father and the kidnapper</i>
<i>were originally acquaintances.</i>

381
00:26:09,000 --> 00:26:11,870
<i>That shouldn't have been</i>
<i>written anywhere, and yet…</i>

382
00:26:13,572 --> 00:26:15,607
The President covered it up?

383
00:26:21,313 --> 00:26:22,881
WHY AN INDEPENDENT COUNTER AT KEIHIN?

384
00:26:30,055 --> 00:26:33,525
EXCLUSIVE INTERVIEW WITH SATORU HATANO
SERIAL KIDNAPPER RELEASED AFTER 25 YEARS

385
00:26:49,074 --> 00:26:51,142
THE DECIDING POINT IN THE GAME

386
00:26:55,246 --> 00:26:56,581
Eight, huh?

387
00:27:02,954 --> 00:27:05,890
MAN FOUND DEAD ON STREET IN SHINAGAWA

388
00:27:06,958 --> 00:27:07,792
NOSE COSMETICS

389
00:27:07,859 --> 00:27:09,361
I'm from Drip &amp; Note.

390
00:27:09,427 --> 00:27:12,430
-Right this way.
-Thank you.

391
00:27:25,343 --> 00:27:26,277
Excuse me.

392
00:27:27,545 --> 00:27:29,147
Have we met somewhere before?

393
00:27:30,382 --> 00:27:32,083
Ah, sorry, sorry.

394
00:27:32,150 --> 00:27:34,219
Not trying to flirt, really.

395
00:27:44,396 --> 00:27:45,397
Um…

396
00:27:46,631 --> 00:27:47,666
Do you need something?

397
00:27:49,200 --> 00:27:50,735
There's something stuck there…

398
00:27:53,471 --> 00:27:54,706
Thank you.

399
00:27:55,473 --> 00:27:56,541
It's cute, though.

400
00:28:03,114 --> 00:28:06,084
What? Yukimura went golfing
with the president?

401
00:28:06,151 --> 00:28:07,018
Yes.

402
00:28:07,085 --> 00:28:10,221
The president was very pleased.
He said he was really good and attentive.

403
00:28:11,489 --> 00:28:13,391
That's surprising for Yukimura.

404
00:28:13,458 --> 00:28:15,994
He seems quiet. So he's on "that side".

405
00:28:17,128 --> 00:28:18,096
What do you mean, "that side"?

406
00:28:18,763 --> 00:28:21,032
The side that thinks
about promotions and stuff.

407
00:28:21,099 --> 00:28:25,070
It's not so easy for an ordinary employee
to get into the president's good graces.

408
00:28:25,136 --> 00:28:28,640
So, he got in through golf. I see, I see.

409
00:28:28,707 --> 00:28:30,775
Why don't you do golf too then, Sano?

410
00:28:30,842 --> 00:28:34,245
What? I have no interest in golf.
Promotions are a hassle anyway.

411
00:28:34,312 --> 00:28:36,181
What's with you?

412
00:28:37,282 --> 00:28:38,616
I mean, it's tough, right?

413
00:28:43,455 --> 00:28:44,656
Manager? Is something wrong?

414
00:28:45,924 --> 00:28:46,958
Nothing.

415
00:28:52,130 --> 00:28:53,832
Ah, let me get that.

416
00:28:57,569 --> 00:28:58,503
Thanks.

417
00:29:03,975 --> 00:29:07,312
-Hello.
-Hello.

418
00:29:16,755 --> 00:29:18,857
Did something happen with Mariko?

419
00:29:21,292 --> 00:29:22,594
I don't know.

420
00:30:07,505 --> 00:30:08,473
I'm sorry.

421
00:30:09,574 --> 00:30:10,475
I'm Sakura.

422
00:30:10,975 --> 00:30:13,044
Um, we met the other day.

423
00:30:16,347 --> 00:30:18,583
-I'm sorry.
-No, no.

424
00:30:19,551 --> 00:30:23,321
I didn't mean to startle you.

425
00:30:24,556 --> 00:30:25,390
It's fine…

426
00:30:25,990 --> 00:30:28,159
I scared you the other day too, didn't I?

427
00:30:30,094 --> 00:30:32,197
You were that detective, right?

428
00:30:32,831 --> 00:30:33,665
Yes.

429
00:30:34,732 --> 00:30:37,368
I was too vague,
saying I'm a civil servant.

430
00:30:37,902 --> 00:30:39,103
I'm sorry.

431
00:30:40,738 --> 00:30:44,709
Of course you can't reveal everything
to someone you just met.

432
00:30:49,681 --> 00:30:50,782
Um…

433
00:30:52,684 --> 00:30:54,185
Can we start over?

434
00:31:02,894 --> 00:31:04,963
My name is Taisuke Sakura.

435
00:31:06,698 --> 00:31:11,135
I work at the Metropolitan
Police Department, Division One.

436
00:31:13,872 --> 00:31:15,306
Twenty years of service.

437
00:31:17,141 --> 00:31:18,009
I am single.

438
00:31:20,645 --> 00:31:23,114
I was hoping to deepen

439
00:31:23,815 --> 00:31:26,317
my acquaintance with you,
Mariko, in my private life.

440
00:31:28,419 --> 00:31:29,487
If you'd like,

441
00:31:30,221 --> 00:31:32,590
how about we have
a meal together sometime?

442
00:32:13,064 --> 00:32:13,898
What?

443
00:32:13,965 --> 00:32:16,134
That's not what we agreed on!

444
00:32:16,734 --> 00:32:17,735
I want our brand to be placed

445
00:32:17,802 --> 00:32:20,772
at an independent counter
at Keihin Department Store.

446
00:32:20,838 --> 00:32:24,142
If it's lumped together with Nose Brand
counters, we'll take customers from--

447
00:32:24,208 --> 00:32:26,945
It's not a bad thing
for the company as a whole.

448
00:32:28,479 --> 00:32:32,383
It will also help acquire
new customers for the existing brands.

449
00:32:32,450 --> 00:32:36,187
VELEL has a different target demographic
from our other brands.

450
00:32:36,254 --> 00:32:38,222
If they are placed side by side,

451
00:32:38,289 --> 00:32:40,425
our brand image will be indecisive!

452
00:32:41,259 --> 00:32:43,895
I cannot give you special treatment.

453
00:32:44,996 --> 00:32:46,264
Special treatment?

454
00:32:52,370 --> 00:32:56,441
Did this project pass
because I'm the president's daughter?

455
00:33:02,814 --> 00:33:05,917
This project passed
because I'm the president's daughter.

456
00:33:05,984 --> 00:33:07,685
I became manager
because I'm your daughter.

457
00:33:07,752 --> 00:33:10,154
I only got into this company
because I'm your daughter.

458
00:33:13,124 --> 00:33:16,794
And because I'm your daughter,
I got kidnapped.

459
00:33:48,059 --> 00:33:49,861
Mariko may be the president's daughter,

460
00:33:49,927 --> 00:33:52,063
but she isn't relying
on special treatment.

461
00:33:55,099 --> 00:33:57,201
Mariko has been fighting forever.

462
00:33:58,669 --> 00:34:00,004
<i>Mariko, hold on.</i>

463
00:34:00,071 --> 00:34:01,172
Wait.

464
00:34:02,607 --> 00:34:03,908
I'll be fine by myself.

465
00:34:04,442 --> 00:34:06,010
The culprit has been caught.

466
00:34:06,077 --> 00:34:07,945
-But…
-I'm off.

467
00:34:09,347 --> 00:34:10,548
Mariko…

468
00:34:19,390 --> 00:34:21,726
Even though she must have been hurt a lot…

469
00:34:24,328 --> 00:34:25,963
she always looked forward…

470
00:34:28,232 --> 00:34:30,101
<i>and fought with her own strength.</i>

471
00:34:34,806 --> 00:34:36,541
It has nothing to do with being
the president's daughter.

472
00:34:36,607 --> 00:34:38,576
Mariko is Mariko…

473
00:34:40,378 --> 00:34:42,146
Nobody understands.

474
00:34:46,984 --> 00:34:49,353
Because I know the real Mariko.

475
00:34:49,420 --> 00:34:52,590
So what if you do?

476
00:34:55,126 --> 00:34:57,462
Just knowing doesn't
change anything, does it?

477
00:34:59,664 --> 00:35:01,466
What do you want to do?

478
00:35:04,168 --> 00:35:05,837
You've loved her for 25 years,

479
00:35:05,903 --> 00:35:07,738
but never had the courage to talk to her.

480
00:35:07,805 --> 00:35:09,307
You've just always watched.

481
00:35:09,373 --> 00:35:12,376
Now you've finally talked to her,
and she's aware of you, right?

482
00:35:18,382 --> 00:35:19,917
So what next?

483
00:36:22,647 --> 00:36:24,949
COSMETICS INGREDIENT GUIDELINE

484
00:36:30,221 --> 00:36:32,623
VELEL SKINCARE - SEPARATE PR CAMPAIGN

485
00:36:32,690 --> 00:36:34,225
SOCIAL MEDIA MARKETING

486
00:36:34,292 --> 00:36:35,893
CHANCE OF SUCCESS, HIGH

487
00:36:39,597 --> 00:36:40,464
Sorry.

488
00:36:42,366 --> 00:36:43,367
This is…

489
00:36:46,304 --> 00:36:49,840
Um, uh, well…

490
00:36:49,907 --> 00:36:52,510
It would be great if we could have

491
00:36:52,577 --> 00:36:55,246
an independent counter
at Keihin Department Store,

492
00:36:55,313 --> 00:36:56,681
but I realized that

493
00:36:56,747 --> 00:37:00,418
we didn't originally think up
the PR plan based on that assumption.

494
00:37:01,385 --> 00:37:04,355
So I looked into

495
00:37:04,422 --> 00:37:09,527
the PR methods used by
hit products in recent years.

496
00:37:09,594 --> 00:37:11,996
EXPERIENCE BOOTH AT TRAIN STATIONS

497
00:37:12,063 --> 00:37:14,532
If we use a selling method
that goes against our intentions

498
00:37:14,599 --> 00:37:19,503
and causes the concept of VELEL
to be conveyed incorrectly to the world,

499
00:37:20,338 --> 00:37:22,807
taking a slow and steady approach

500
00:37:23,908 --> 00:37:26,110
might be the better option.

501
00:37:29,247 --> 00:37:33,484
Ah, but it would mean going
against the president's wishes,

502
00:37:33,551 --> 00:37:36,220
so that might cause trouble
for you, Manager…

503
00:37:41,225 --> 00:37:43,194
I misunderstood you.

504
00:37:45,496 --> 00:37:47,265
I thought you

505
00:37:47,331 --> 00:37:50,401
just wanted my father to like you
to advance your career.

506
00:37:51,869 --> 00:37:56,007
That's why you were working hard
in this department and being nice to me.

507
00:37:59,744 --> 00:38:00,645
But…

508
00:38:02,079 --> 00:38:05,583
you actually have pure intentions.

509
00:38:07,151 --> 00:38:11,088
I'm the one
who assumed everyone only cares about me

510
00:38:12,323 --> 00:38:14,325
because I'm the president's daughter.

511
00:38:15,926 --> 00:38:18,729
I failed to actually look at you
as a person.

512
00:38:20,898 --> 00:38:21,966
I'm sorry.

513
00:38:27,505 --> 00:38:30,508
Actually, I was thinking
the exact same thing.

514
00:38:31,208 --> 00:38:32,943
A PR method suited for VELEL…

515
00:38:33,010 --> 00:38:35,046
I want to help!

516
00:38:38,049 --> 00:38:39,483
I want to help

517
00:38:40,918 --> 00:38:42,586
and be by your side, Manager.

518
00:38:44,655 --> 00:38:48,159
I'm so surprised that a time
like this would come in my life,

519
00:38:48,225 --> 00:38:50,728
and it's so unbelievable,

520
00:38:50,795 --> 00:38:54,298
but I'm happy just to be here right now.

521
00:38:56,634 --> 00:38:58,969
That's why I want to work hard.

522
00:39:00,237 --> 00:39:01,739
Being able to be here

523
00:39:01,806 --> 00:39:04,442
makes me the happiest
I've ever been in my life.

524
00:39:07,545 --> 00:39:08,979
What…

525
00:39:09,046 --> 00:39:11,248
"Happiest in your life"?
What an exaggeration…

526
00:39:17,421 --> 00:39:18,356
But…

527
00:39:21,692 --> 00:39:22,593
Thank you.

528
00:39:43,080 --> 00:39:45,549
<i>I want to be of use to Mariko.</i>

529
00:39:46,484 --> 00:39:50,321
<i>Just so that Mariko can live pleasantly</i>
<i>and happily.</i>

530
00:39:51,355 --> 00:39:52,590
<i>That's all.</i>

531
00:39:53,624 --> 00:39:55,159
UNIVERSITY ENTRANCE EXAM SITE

532
00:39:55,226 --> 00:39:56,060
<i>That's all I want.</i>

533
00:40:12,476 --> 00:40:14,645
ENTRANCE EXAM ADMISSION TICKET

534
00:40:26,857 --> 00:40:27,925
Hey, you!

535
00:40:28,726 --> 00:40:30,661
You dropped this.

536
00:40:31,962 --> 00:40:33,431
Thank you very much.

537
00:40:57,121 --> 00:41:00,424
<i>I want to be of use to Mariko.</i>

538
00:41:03,594 --> 00:41:06,030
GINJIRO NOSE

539
00:41:07,965 --> 00:41:09,834
GINJIRO NOSE

540
00:41:12,536 --> 00:41:13,504
HIDEO JINNO

541
00:41:13,571 --> 00:41:16,607
<i>These two have been together</i>
<i>for more than half a century,</i>

542
00:41:16,674 --> 00:41:18,275
<i>but they both went</i>

543
00:41:18,342 --> 00:41:20,144
<i>to different high schools</i>
<i>and universities.</i>

544
00:41:21,579 --> 00:41:24,114
<i>Which means, they go back</i>
<i>further than that…</i>

545
00:41:26,917 --> 00:41:28,719
HIDEO JINNO

546
00:41:28,786 --> 00:41:30,054
HIDEO JINNO

547
00:41:30,120 --> 00:41:31,555
SEE ALL PHOTOS

548
00:41:36,894 --> 00:41:38,329
WITH GIN-CHAN IN OUR OLD HANGOUT
FIRST TIME IN A WHILE!

549
00:41:41,098 --> 00:41:42,233
HOSEN

550
00:41:49,874 --> 00:41:52,443
-Thank you!
-See you!

551
00:41:52,510 --> 00:41:54,411
-Take care! Thank you!
-Thank you!

552
00:41:56,280 --> 00:41:57,181
All right.

553
00:41:57,781 --> 00:41:59,950
All right, all right.

554
00:42:02,920 --> 00:42:04,555
Excuse me.

555
00:42:04,622 --> 00:42:05,556
Yes?

556
00:42:06,757 --> 00:42:08,392
This is all I have…

557
00:42:08,459 --> 00:42:10,761
Wow, thank you so much.

558
00:42:10,828 --> 00:42:15,165
I had no idea Nose's son
had grown this big.

559
00:42:15,799 --> 00:42:18,102
And you're planning
a surprise celebration?

560
00:42:18,168 --> 00:42:19,370
He'd be so happy!

561
00:42:20,237 --> 00:42:22,973
I wonder if I have
anything else interesting?

562
00:42:23,040 --> 00:42:24,074
Wait there a second!

563
00:42:24,141 --> 00:42:26,777
Oh, thank you so much.

564
00:42:27,278 --> 00:42:29,380
YEAR 6, CLASS ONE - FRIENDS FOREVER

565
00:42:33,651 --> 00:42:35,920
HIDEO JINNO

566
00:42:35,986 --> 00:42:39,490
GINJIRO NOSE

567
00:42:41,792 --> 00:42:43,627
YEAR 6, CLASS 2
SEE YOU AGAIN AT THE GRADUATION PARTY

568
00:42:45,529 --> 00:42:47,364
YEAR 6, CLASS 3
NO. 1 GOLD STAR CLASS

569
00:42:51,235 --> 00:42:52,069
Satoru…

570
00:42:52,136 --> 00:42:54,872
SATORU HATANO

571
00:42:56,240 --> 00:42:59,009
<i>Mariko's kidnapping was not a coincidence.</i>

572
00:43:21,799 --> 00:43:24,635
<i>I won't forgive anyone who jeopardizes…</i>

573
00:43:26,270 --> 00:43:27,204
<i>Mariko's happiness.</i>

574
00:43:34,311 --> 00:43:36,847
METROPOLITAN POLICE

575
00:43:46,624 --> 00:43:50,961
It's strange that the camera
has one blind spot

576
00:43:51,028 --> 00:43:52,696
exactly where the crime scene is.

577
00:43:56,266 --> 00:43:57,101
Hey, look.

578
00:43:58,102 --> 00:44:00,437
This is right in front of the crime scene.

579
00:44:02,106 --> 00:44:04,208
Taken right before
the estimated time of death.

580
00:44:10,280 --> 00:44:11,515
Who is this man?

581
00:44:27,665 --> 00:44:28,499
Excuse me.

582
00:44:30,067 --> 00:44:31,835
You're Sota Yukimura, right?

583
00:44:34,605 --> 00:44:37,708
May I speak with you for a moment?

584
00:44:43,147 --> 00:44:45,582
<i>I want Mariko to be happy.</i>

585
00:44:46,884 --> 00:44:48,185
<i>That's all.</i>

586
00:44:53,724 --> 00:44:55,292
<i>So,</i>

587
00:44:59,029 --> 00:45:00,864
<i>you don't need to know anything.</i>

588
00:45:01,532 --> 00:45:03,400
NEXT TIME…

589
00:45:04,968 --> 00:45:07,905
Subtitle translation by: Maslin Friedman
